  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThis came out of a breakout with @keithamus and @westbrook.\nAuthors often need to know the computed role of an element, but booting the accessibility engine for `element.computedRole` is slow.\nWhat if we made it easier to implement in userland? The part that is tricky is the static data that UAs already have: what is the default role for each element type? \n\nThe proposal is to introduce a new `element.defaultRole` IDL attribute which returns:\n- The element's default mapped role for built-ins (e.g. `heading` on `<h1>`)\n- `ElementInternals.role` for custom elements (or the default role for custom elements if no `ElementInternals`)\n\nThen the computed role becomes basically:\n\n```js\nlet computedRole = element.role || element.defaultRole;\n```",
